{
  "openapi": "3.1.1",
  "info": {
    "title": "OpenAsy Backups API",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "summary": "Whether your backups ran, how late they are, and whether anyone has restored one.",
    "description": "Every screen of backups uses this API, and so can your scripts (ADR 0014). Within `/api/v1` changes are additive only; anything removed is deprecated first (ADR 0024). Errors use Problem Details (RFC 9457).\n\nBackups tracks backup jobs; it makes no backups. Jobs report their runs and restore tests with `BACKUPS_INGEST_TOKEN`. Everything else takes the session of a signed-in person or an API token, and each operation names the role it needs (`x-openasy-role`: viewer, editor, admin; ADR 0003).\n\nSign-in, members and API tokens are under `/api/v1/auth`, provided by [@openasy/auth](https://github.com/openasy/auth#routes).",
    "license": {
      "name": "AGPL-3.0-only",
      "identifier": "AGPL-3.0-only"
    }
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "/",
      "description": "This backups"
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Reports",
      "description": "What jobs and restore tests send."
    },
    {
      "name": "Jobs",
      "description": "What makes backups, and how it is doing."
    },
    {
      "name": "Settings",
      "description": "When a job counts as late, failing or untested."
    },
    {
      "name": "Product",
      "description": "Version and overview of this backups."
    }
  ],
  "paths": {
    "/api/v1/runs": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "reportRun",
        "tags": [
          "Reports"
        ],
        "summary": "Report a run",
        "security": [
          {
            "ingestToken": []
          },
          {
            "session": []
          },
          {
            "apiToken": []
          },
          {
            "adminToken": []
          }
        ],
        "description": "Reports one finished run of a job. The body is our own JSON, `{ job, startedAt, endedAt, status, snapshotId?, sizeBytes?, filesNew?, filesChanged?, error? }`, or what the tool prints: the summary of `restic backup --json` (the last line is found among the lines it prints), or a Velero `Backup` resource once its phase is Completed, PartiallyFailed or Failed. A job nobody defined is refused unless an admin allows reports to create jobs. The same snapshot twice is the same run.\n\n```bash\nrestic backup --json /srv | tail -n 1 | curl -sf -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $BACKUPS_INGEST_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' --data-binary @- \"https://backups.example.com/api/v1/runs?job=files\"\nkubectl -n velero get backup nightly-20261022 -o json | curl -sf -X POST -H \"Authorization: Bearer $BACKUPS_INGEST_TOKEN\" \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' --data-binary @- \"https://backups.example.com/api/v1/runs?job=cluster\"\n```\n\nThe body may be gzipped, up to 4 MiB unpacked.\n\nTakes BACKUPS_INGEST_TOKEN, or an API token with the editor role.",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "name": "job",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "The job's name, when the body does not say.",
            "schema": {
              "type": "string",
              "maxLength": 128
            }
          },
          {
            "name": "tool",
            "in": "query",
            "required": false,
            "description": "restic, velero or other. Set when auto-create makes the job.",
            "schema": {
              "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Tool"
            }
          }
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "required": true,
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "Our own report, a restic summary or a Velero Backup."
              }
            }
          }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": {
            "description": "The snapshot was reported before; nothing changed.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Run"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "201": {
            "description": "Kept. `x-job-state` holds the job's state now.",
            "content": {
              "application/json": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Run"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "400": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "401": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "403": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "413": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "422": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          },
          "503": {
            "$ref": "#/components/responses/Problem"
          }
        },
        "x-openasy-role": "editor"
      }
    },
    "/api/v1/restore-tests": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "reportRestoreTest",
        "tags": [
          "Reports"
        ],
        "summary": "Report a restore test",
